## Add-by-RSS surface ownership

My Library's Add by RSS screen is the **library for those feeds**: chips for podcasts, episodes,
artists, albums, tracks, and livestreams; a plus that opens the add form; pull-to-refresh that
refreshes only add-by-RSS feeds. Channel detail and credentials editing stay on the **Library**
stack (`AddByRssPodcastDetail`, `AddByRssCredentials`, `AddByRssAdd`).

- Home lists directory follows and ready add-by-RSS follows together on every chip. Home shows
  no Needs username and password section; a feed waiting on a username and password shows only in
  the Add by RSS library. An add-by-RSS row on Home opens Home's own `AddByRssPodcastDetail`,
  `AddByRssEpisodeDetail` for an episode, or `AddByRssLivestreamDetail` for a livestream. The
  library opens those same screens on the Library stack.
- Do **not** jump to the Home stack to open an add-by-RSS feed's detail from Library.
- The Add by RSS detail and credentials screens are also registered on Browse and Search, because
  a directory artist page there lists the member's Add by RSS albums. A row opened there pushes
  on that tab's stack.
- The full player's item title and channel title are the exception. A directory follow opens on
  Home. Content this device does not follow opens on Browse. Add by RSS is a follow, so those
  links open Home's add-by-RSS detail. The item title opens the channel page and then the item
  page on that same stack, so Back from the item returns to the channel. The channel title opens
  the channel page only. A flow that starts in Search, Library, or Browse still pushes on that
  tab's own stack.
- CarPlay and Android Auto keep add-by-RSS follows in the native library index (no separate Add by
  RSS screen there).
- Web Subscribed (`/`) lists directory follows and this browser's ready add-by-RSS follows
  together; Clips stays directory only. The web Add by RSS library is one page, `/add-by-rss`,
  linked from the sidebar's Library section.
